    "title": "Cricket India Squad",
    "text": "• Jasprit Bumrah and Ravindra Jadeja have been named in India’s test squad for the upcoming tour of Sri Lanka.\n• The two tests will be played in Galle and Colombo starting August 15.\n• The tests are part of the 2025-27 World Test Championship.\n• India is currently fifth in the table with Sri Lanka sixth.\n• Bumrah and batter Sai Sudharsan will undergo fitness tests ahead of joining the touring party.\n• Indian selectors have called up 33-year-old Saransh Jain to replace the injured Washington Sundar.\n• Shubman Gill continues leading the side with Lokesh Rahul as vice-captain.\n• Rishabh Pant and Dhruv Jurel are the designated wicketkeepers.",
    "summary": "- Bikas Das - AP Star pace bowler Jasprit Bumrah and all-rounder Ravindra Jadeja have been named in India’s test squad for the upcoming tour of Sri Lanka. Bumrah and batter Sai Sudharsan will undergo fitness tests ahead of joining the touring party. Indian selectors also call up 33-year-old Saransh Jain to replace the injured Washington Sundar. Shubman Gill continues leading the side with Lokesh Rahul as vice-captain. We'd love to hear eyewitness accounts, the history behind an article.",
